| editorial =
'''The audit and the line'''

The audit began today. 12,000 workers lined up at a temporary office in Isshinji. The first claim was processed at 8:15 AM. The line formed at 6:00 AM.

The line is the story. Not the audit. The audit is procedure. The line is people. People who paid into a pension fund for years and do not know if their money exists. People who trusted a system that was emptying their savings while telling them everything was fine.

The audit will take weeks. The line will take longer. The workers will go home and wait. The IAA Commission will investigate. The prosecution will build its case. The hearing is July 17. The system is moving. The workers are waiting. Both are happening at the same time.

